{"type":"text","timestamp":1792483442909,"sessionID":"ses_ea7ae49edffeqHl0eGUfeYjbPJ","part":{"id":"prt_15856b486001uOtRZWlFb39HkC","messageID":"msg_15855d102001WR4wVuG9JrcnXP","sessionID":"ses_ea7ae49edffeqHl0eGUfeYjbPJ","type":"text","text":"\n\nNext, I'll fix a subtle strictness issue: in `ring_buf_count`/`ring_buf_is_full`, the raw `int32_t` counter results are being subtracted before being cast (which, in theory, could become signed overflow after 2^31 writes). I'll make them match the `uint32_t` difference used in the write/read paths. Also, I'll skip the redundant self-store when the bulk transfer count is 0.\n\n","time":{"start":1792483439750,"end":1792483442890}}}
